This repository is a release snapshot of a Lean 4 formalization of Theorem 1.1 and Corollary 1.2 of
the PSI paper "The vacuum Bell correlation of the massive free scalar field attains the classical bound for bounded regions beyond a finite separation", with the CHSH inequality for two bounded regions moved apart along
a fixed spacelike direction or by spatial translations (Problem 12 of the IQOQI Vienna Open Quantum
Problems). The Lean files under VacuumBellSeparation/ are taken from PSI's development repository,
with the Lean module-system header added, declarations made public and Mathlib imports added as
the module system requires, and comment edits, among them corrections of comments that cite the
paper of record; the modules VacuumBellSeparation/FreeField/OQP12.lean
and VacuumBellSeparation/Audit/FinalCheck.lean and the files Challenge.lean, Solution.lean and
VacuumBellSeparation.lean are new.

Comparator checks that the theorems proved in
Solution.lean are exactly the statements in Challenge.lean, using only the three standard axioms,
and the proofs are replayed by Lean's kernel and by independent kernels.

Provenance and use of AI. This result was released by Physical Superintelligence (PSI). The
mathematics was developed by PSI researchers working with AI models (OpenAI's GPT-6-Astra and
GPT-5.6 Pro and Anthropic's Claude Fable 5.1) in automated research workflows at PSI. The Lean
formalization was written by AI agents (Anthropic's Claude Opus 5.5 in Claude Code, and OpenAI's GPT-6-Astra in Codex) under PSI's direction. David
Turturean is responsible for the correctness of the paper. The paper's AI disclosure has the
details; formalization.yaml records which agent did which part.

